Packaging v7unix-toolchain for Distributions
============================================

This file is for distribution packagers who want to add v7unix-toolchain to
their distro's package repository.  Template packaging files for several
systems are provided under `dist/`.  Each is roughly 90% complete — the
packager fills in maintainer details, changelog, and distro-specific
adjustments.

What v7unix-toolchain Is
------------------------

v7unix-toolchain is a modern-host port of the Seventh Edition (V7) Unix
PDP-11 C toolchain — the `cc` driver, its `cpp`/`c0`/`c1`/`c2` passes, the
`as`/`as2` assembler, and the `ld` linker — that cross-compiles PDP-11 code
from a modern 64-bit host.  Distributed under the Caldera "Ancient UNIX"
license (see `COPYING`).

Dependencies
------------

Build-time (all in every distro's base toolchain):
  - a C99 compiler — `gcc`, `clang`, or `pcc` (the `modern/` sources build
    with all three)
  - `bison` (for the `cpp` pass's `#if` grammar)
  - `python3` (regenerates the `c2` pass from its single `c2.c` source)
  - GNU `make`

  `configure` is shipped, so `autoconf`/`automake` are **not** needed to build
  — only to regenerate the build system from `configure.ac`/`Makefile.am`.

Runtime:
  - no shared libraries; the tools are standalone host binaries.
  - the PDP-11 target runtime (`crt0.o`, `libc.a`) installs as plain data.

How the Build Works
-------------------

Standard autotools:

    ./configure --prefix=/usr [--libexecdir=... --libdir=...]
    make
    make install DESTDIR=...

Install layout (every location configurable via the standard `./configure`
flags; the three data dirs carry a `v7unix` suffix):

    $(libexecdir)/v7unix/     the 8 host binaries (cc, cpp, c0, c1, c2, as,
                              as2, ld) under their original V7 names
    $(bindir)/                v7cc, v7as, v7ld — symlinks to the above
    $(libdir)/v7unix/         the PDP-11 target runtime (crt0.o, libc.a)
    $(mandir)/v7unix/man1/    the V7 manual pages (cc.1, as.1, ld.1, lex.1,
                              yacc.1, make.1, adb.1)
    $(mandir)/man1/           v7cc.1, v7as.1, v7ld.1 — `.so` stubs into v7unix

The one cross-distro divergence is where "internal executables" live: the
BSDs and Red Hat/Gentoo use a dedicated `libexec` dir; Debian and Arch do not
and put package-private programs under `/usr/lib`.  Because the package ships
no *host* libraries (everything under `$(libdir)/v7unix` is PDP-11 target
data), the templates pin `--libdir` to a non-multiarch `/usr/lib`:

    System                       --libexecdir          --libdir (x86_64)
    ---------------------------  -------------------  -------------------
    FreeBSD / OpenBSD / NetBSD   /usr/local/libexec    /usr/local/lib
    Red Hat / Fedora / RHEL      /usr/libexec          /usr/lib64
    Gentoo                       /usr/libexec          /usr/lib64
    Debian / Ubuntu              /usr/lib/v7unix       /usr/lib
    Arch                         /usr/lib/v7unix       /usr/lib
    Alpine / Slackware           /usr/lib/v7unix       /usr/lib

(The `v7unix` suffix is appended by `configure` to whatever `--libexecdir` /
`--libdir` it is given, so `/usr/lib/v7unix` above is `--libexecdir=/usr/lib`.)

Per-Distribution Notes
======================

RPM (Fedora / RHEL / CentOS)
----------------------------

  Files:  dist/rpm/v7unix-toolchain.spec

  Customize: URL/Source0 if hosting your own tarball, the %changelog entry.
  Build:  rpmbuild -ba dist/rpm/v7unix-toolchain.spec
  Submit: Fedora Package Review process / EPEL.

Debian / Ubuntu
---------------

  Files:  dist/debian/

  Customize: debian/changelog, debian/control Maintainer field, debian/copyright.
  Build:  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc
  Submit: File an ITP against wnpp.

Arch Linux
----------

  Files:  dist/arch/PKGBUILD

  Customize: Maintainer line, sha256sums (updpkgsums).
  Build:  makepkg -si
  Submit: AUR.

Alpine Linux
------------

  Files:  dist/alpine/APKBUILD

  Customize: Maintainer line, sha512sums (abuild checksum).
  Build:  abuild -r
  Submit: MR against aports.git.

FreeBSD
-------

  Files:  dist/freebsd/

  Customize: MAINTAINER email, distinfo (real SHA256/SIZE).
  Build:  make -C dist/freebsd install (in a ports tree)
  Submit: FreeBSD bug / send-pr, category "ports".

OpenBSD
-------

  Files:  dist/openbsd/

  Customize: MAINTAINER email, pkg/PLIST after a test install.
  Build:  make -C dist/openbsd install (in a ports tree)
  Submit: diff to ports@openbsd.org.

NetBSD
------

  Files:  dist/netbsd/

  Customize: MAINTAINER email, distinfo (make distinfo).
  Build:  bmake install (in a pkgsrc tree)
  Submit: diff to pkgsrc-wip / pkgsrc-changes.

Gentoo
------

  Files:  dist/gentoo/

  Customize: metadata.xml maintainer, ebuild SRC_URI, KEYWORDS.
  Build:  ebuild dist/gentoo/v7unix-toolchain-0.1.0.ebuild manifest && emerge
  Submit: bug at bugs.gentoo.org (category "Ebuild") or the GURU overlay.

NixOS
-----

  Files:  dist/nixos/default.nix

  Customize: fetchFromGitHub owner/hash, meta.maintainers.
  Build:  nix-build -E 'with import <nixpkgs> {}; callPackage ./dist/nixos/default.nix {}'
  Submit: PR against nixpkgs.

Slackware
---------

  Files:  dist/slackware/

  Customize: seatuya.SlackBuild copyright, seatuya.info MD5SUM/MAINTAINER, slack-desc URL.
  Build:  source v7unix-toolchain.info && sh v7unix-toolchain.SlackBuild
  Submit: SlackBuilds.org (SBo).
